  "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-cheri/issues/863",
  "number": 863,
  "state": "closed",
  "locked": false,
  "title": "Svucrg: Reword PTE bits extension.",
  "user": {
    "login": "qwattash",
    "id": 1173169,
    "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjExNzMxNjk=",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1173169?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/qwattash",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/qwattash/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": " - The CRW field is extended to 3 bits. The CD and CRG bits are logical states encoded by the CRW field instead of proper separate bits in the PTE.\r\n - Clarify Reserved states for PTE.U=0. This should make it easier to add extensions that define CRW states that do not imply any CD/CRG semantics, for example a kernel revocation extension can define a cap-permissive state without load-side faults.\r\n - Flip the polarity of the encoded \"PTE.CD\" bit (PTE.CRW[1]), this ensures that software unaware of the Svucrg extension can continue to use the CRW bit with the exact same semantic.",
  "created_at": "2025-11-27T11:23:21Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-11-27T17:22:23Z",
  "closed_at": "2025-11-27T17:22:23Z",
